.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH gpuq-run 1  "gpuq 0.2.0" 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
gpuq\-run \- Run a command under a GPU lease
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgpuq run\fR [\fB\-\-api\fR] [\fB\-\-class\fR] [\fB\-\-vram\fR] [\fB\-\-name\fR] [\fB\-\-yieldable\fR] [\fB\-\-yield\-signal\fR] [\fB\-\-card\fR] [\fB\-\-fallback\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fICMD\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run a command under a GPU lease
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-api\fR \fI<HOST:PORT>\fR
Address of the gpuq control API (default: $GPUQ_API, else 127.0.0.1:9390)
.TP
\fB\-\-class\fR \fI<CLASS>\fR [default: batch]
Priority class from gpuq\*(Aqs [classes] table
.TP
\fB\-\-vram\fR \fI<VRAM>\fR [default: all]
VRAM to reserve, e.g. 8G, 3000M or all
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Lease name shown in `gpuq status` (default: the command\*(Aqs basename)
.TP
\fB\-\-yieldable\fR
Signal the job when something more important needs the card
.TP
\fB\-\-yield\-signal\fR \fI<SIGNAL>\fR
Signal sent on a yield request, e.g. SIGUSR1 or TERM. Default: gpuq\*(Aqs `[run] yield_signal`, else SIGUSR1
.TP
\fB\-\-card\fR \fI<NAME|any>\fR
Card to run on: a name from `gpuq status`, or `any` for the first card with room. Default: the primary card
.TP
\fB\-\-fallback\fR
If gpuq is not running, run the command anyway
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
[\fICMD\fR]
The command, after `\-\-`
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgpuq\fR(1)
